//! Persistent collections: every operation returns a new version and
//! leaves the old one intact and usable.
//!
//! - `list` — a singly linked list.
//! - `rtqueue` — a FIFO queue with worst-case constant-time operations.
//! - `fingertree` — a random-access sequence: both ends, indexing,
//!   splitting, and concatenation.
//! - `hashmap`, `hashset` — hash-based maps and sets with persistent updates.
//! - `wavlset`, `wavlmap` — ordered set and map on a balanced tree.
//! - `pairing_heap`, `binomial_heap` — min-priority queues.
//!
//! The two priority queues implement the same API and differ in which
//! usage they are fast for. Reach for `pairing_heap` by default: it is
//! the faster queue when each version is used once and discarded, which
//! is what queue code normally does. Reach for `binomial_heap` when old
//! versions are kept and operated on again, or when the cost of a single
//! operation matters — its bounds are worst case, where the pairing
//! heap's are amortized and degrade sharply if a version is reused.
//! Each module's header gives the concrete cases and the measurements.

pub mod binomial_heap;
pub mod fingertree;
pub mod hashmap;
pub mod hashset;
pub mod list;
pub mod pairing_heap;
pub mod rtqueue;
pub mod wavlmap;
pub mod wavlset;
